{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016F5xSXs28UmL9ESjNyA9ZW","type":"tool_result","content":"394\t\\section*{Limitations}\n395\t\n396\tOur study has three main limitations.\n397\tFirst, the cross-scale evidence is incomplete: Qwen3-8B training failed due to computational constraints, leaving the capacity threshold hypothesis untested at larger scales.\n398\tSecond, all experiments use a single model family (Qwen3); generalization to other architectures remains unverified, though the Goodhart mechanism (\\isr{}'s inherent tautology bias) is architecture-independent.\n399\tThird, \\isr{} measures syntactic necessity rather than semantic faithfulness---premises that are syntactically necessary may still be semantically vacuous---bounding \\sta{}'s diagnostic scope to structural quality.\n400\t\n401\t\\bibliographystyle{acl_natbib}\n402\t\\begin{thebibliography}{10}\n403\t\n404\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Amodei et~al.}2016]{amodei2016concrete}\n405\tDario Amodei, Chris Olah, Jacob Steinhardt, Paul Christiano, John Schulman, and Dan Man\\'{e}.\n406\t\\newblock 2016.\n407\t\\newblock Concrete problems in AI safety.\n408\t\\newblock {\\em arXiv preprint arXiv:1606.06565}.\n409\t\n410\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Covert et~al.}2021]{covert2021explaining}\n411\tIan Covert, Scott Lundberg, and Su-In Lee.\n412\t\\newblock 2021.\n413\t\\newblock Explaining by removing: A unified framework for model explanation.\n414\t\\newblock {\\em Journal of Machine Learning Research}, 22(209):1--90.\n415\t\n416\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Gao et~al.}2023]{gao2023scaling}\n417\tLeo Gao, John Schulman, and Jacob Hilton.\n418\t\\newblock 2023.\n419\t\\newblock Scaling laws for reward model overoptimization.\n420\t\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of ICML}.\n421\t\n422\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Luo et~al.}2024]{luo2024improve}\n423\tHaipeng Luo, Qingfeng Sun, Can Xu, Pu Zhao, Jianguang Lou, Chongyang Tao, Xiubo Geng, Qingwei Lin, Shifeng Chen, and Dongmei Zhang.\n424\t\\newblock 2024.\n425\t\\newblock Wizardmath: Empowering mathematical reasoning for large language models via reinforced evol-instruct.\n426\t\\newblock {\\em arXiv preprint arXiv:2308.09583}.\n427\t\n428\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Pan et~al.}2022]{pan2022effects}\n429\tAlexander Pan, Kush Bhatia, and Jacob Steinhardt.\n430\t\\newblock 2022.\n431\t\\newblock The effects of reward misspecification: Mapping and mitigating misaligned models.\n432\t\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of ICLR}.\n433\t\n434\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Shao et~al.}2024]{shao2024deepseekmath}\n435\tZhihong Shao, Peiyi Wang, Qihao Zhu, Runxin Xu, Junxiao Song, Mingchuan Zhang, Y.K. Li, Y. Wu, and Daya Guo.\n436\t\\newblock 2024.\n437\t\\newblock Deepseekmath: Pushing the limits of mathematical reasoning in open language models.\n438\t\\newblock {\\em arXiv preprint arXiv:2402.03300}.\n439\t\n440\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Skalse et~al.}2022]{skalse2022defining}\n441\tJoar Skalse, Nikolaus Howe, Dmitrii Krasheninnikov, and David Krueger.\n442\t\\newblock 2022.\n443\t\\newblock Defining and characterizing reward hacking.\n444\t\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of NeurIPS}.\n445\t\n446\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Wang et~al.}2024]{wang2024math}\n447\tPeiyi Wang, Lei Li, Zhihong Shao, R.X. Xu, Damai Dai, Yifei Li, Deli Chen, Y. Wu, and Zhifang Sui.\n448\t\\newblock 2024.\n449\t\\newblock Math-shepherd: Verify and reinforce llms step-by-step without human annotations.\n450\t\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of ACL}.\n451\t\n452\t\\end{thebibliography}\n453\t\n454\t\\end{document}\n455\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cb2d99a-0b75-4c41-b0e5-5d0dc9a6bce0","uuid":"af17ad40-c0dd-4fa1-80d9-f48c7a0664f2","timestamp":"2026-05-21T22:42:44.683Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T214001/worst/paper.tex","content":"\\section*{Limitations}\n\nOur study has three main limitations.\nFirst, the cross-scale evidence is incomplete: Qwen3-8B training failed due to computational constraints, leaving the capacity threshold hypothesis untested at larger scales.\nSecond, all experiments use a single model family (Qwen3); generalization to other architectures remains unverified, though the Goodhart mechanism (\\isr{}'s inherent tautology bias) is architecture-independent.\nThird, \\isr{} measures syntactic necessity rather than semantic faithfulness---premises that are syntactically necessary may still be semantically vacuous---bounding \\sta{}'s diagnostic scope to structural quality.\n\n\\bibliographystyle{acl_natbib}\n\\begin{thebibliography}{10}\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Amodei et~al.}2016]{amodei2016concrete}\nDario Amodei, Chris Olah, Jacob Steinhardt, Paul Christiano, John Schulman, and Dan Man\\'{e}.\n\\newblock 2016.\n\\newblock Concrete problems in AI safety.\n\\newblock {\\em arXiv preprint arXiv:1606.06565}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Covert et~al.}2021]{covert2021explaining}\nIan Covert, Scott Lundberg, and Su-In Lee.\n\\newblock 2021.\n\\newblock Explaining by removing: A unified framework for model explanation.\n\\newblock {\\em Journal of Machine Learning Research}, 22(209):1--90.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Gao et~al.}2023]{gao2023scaling}\nLeo Gao, John Schulman, and Jacob Hilton.\n\\newblock 2023.\n\\newblock Scaling laws for reward model overoptimization.\n\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of ICML}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Luo et~al.}2024]{luo2024improve}\nHaipeng Luo, Qingfeng Sun, Can Xu, Pu Zhao, Jianguang Lou, Chongyang Tao, Xiubo Geng, Qingwei Lin, Shifeng Chen, and Dongmei Zhang.\n\\newblock 2024.\n\\newblock Wizardmath: Empowering mathematical reasoning for large language models via reinforced evol-instruct.\n\\newblock {\\em arXiv preprint arXiv:2308.09583}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Pan et~al.}2022]{pan2022effects}\nAlexander Pan, Kush Bhatia, and Jacob Steinhardt.\n\\newblock 2022.\n\\newblock The effects of reward misspecification: Mapping and mitigating misaligned models.\n\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of ICLR}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Shao et~al.}2024]{shao2024deepseekmath}\nZhihong Shao, Peiyi Wang, Qihao Zhu, Runxin Xu, Junxiao Song, Mingchuan Zhang, Y.K. Li, Y. Wu, and Daya Guo.\n\\newblock 2024.\n\\newblock Deepseekmath: Pushing the limits of mathematical reasoning in open language models.\n\\newblock {\\em arXiv preprint arXiv:2402.03300}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Skalse et~al.}2022]{skalse2022defining}\nJoar Skalse, Nikolaus Howe, Dmitrii Krasheninnikov, and David Krueger.\n\\newblock 2022.\n\\newblock Defining and characterizing reward hacking.\n\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of NeurIPS}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Wang et~al.}2024]{wang2024math}\nPeiyi Wang, Lei Li, Zhihong Shao, R.X. Xu, Damai Dai, Yifei Li, Deli Chen, Y. Wu, and Zhifang Sui.\n\\newblock 2024.\n\\newblock Math-shepherd: Verify and reinforce llms step-by-step without human annotations.\n\\newblock In {\\em Proceedings of ACL}.\n\n\\end{thebibliography}\n\n\\end{document}\n","numLines":62,"startLine":394,"totalLines":455}}}
